Z||000003||AkursedX||12-09-2000||01:17 PM||||This car was in Car and Driver a while back.  It also competed in their One Lap of America competition.  I believed it had to drop out though because of cooling problems but don't quote me on that.  <BR>Needless to say, it is a nice idea, but personally, I think the car looks very ugly.  That enormous rear end does nothing for me.  But I wouldn't mind having 600hp  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||12-09-2000||02:47 PM||||The gear ratios are slightly different between the 2 trannys so they don't shift at the same time. The rear engine can be shut off too if I remember correctly.||||reg||1
Z||000005||PearlBlueSoul||12-09-2000||03:00 PM||||Yah, I was about to say I saw that in a magazine.  I remember Motor Trend diong a piece on it I think.  Think about that tho:  dual gauge pods, watching 2 tachs climb up and down independantly.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  cool stuff.  the rear motor is the 300HP version and the front is a 275 version of caddy's northstar V8.  <P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
